-- title:
--   Stability of finite and toric points under an endomorphism over A
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a nonzero level $M$ with $p \mid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$. Let $\Lambda$ be level data for $(p,M,H)$ over $A$, consisting of a morphism $\sigma_A \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to \operatorname{Spec} \mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ with $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point composite equal to the generic point $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$, a scheme $X$ with structure morphism $\Lambda.f$ over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ carrying a relative group law, and parametrisations of its generic and special points; and let $O$ be a level-$\Gamma_H(M)$ Néron object at $p$ attached to $\Lambda$, with structure morphism $g \colon G \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$, relative group law $O.L$ and bijection $O.\mathrm{pts}$ from $J_H(M) = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the level-$H$ function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ onto the generic points of $g$. Let $W$ be an endomorphism of the base change $G_A = G \times_{\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}} \operatorname{Spec} A$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, assumed by hypothesis to be additive for the base-changed group law on points over every $\operatorname{Spec} A$-scheme, and let $w \colon J_H(M) \to J_H(M)$ be an additive map which, hypothesis by hypothesis, induces on each point $O.\mathrm{pts}(x)$ the composite with $W$ of its transport to a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of $G_A$, read back as a generic point of $g$. The conclusion is twofold: first, for every $m$, $w$ maps the subgroup $O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ — generated by the classes of $m$-torsion in $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ whose associated generic point extends to a point over $\sigma_A$ — into itself; second, if $\Lambda.f$ satisfies the abelian-scheme property bundle over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ (smooth, proper, connected fibres, and admitting a relative group law), then for every $m > 0$ the subgroup $O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$ generated by the toric points of level $m$ is likewise stable under $w$.
--
--   This is the stability statement for the finite and toric subgroups of $J_H(M)$ under an endomorphism of the Néron object defined over the place $A$ rather than over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$, which is what allows operators such as the Fricke involution at level $\Gamma_H(M)$ to be treated alongside the Hecke and diamond operators. It is used in the construction of the toric-finite filtration of the Tate module of $J_H(M)$ and in the counting arguments comparing corners and toric parts that feed the level-lowering step.
